  "answer": {
    "response": "The export request flows unchanged through GraphQL and BullMQ:\n\n`ExportResolver.requestExport` → `ExportProducer.enqueue` → `ExportJob` payload → `ExportProcessor.process` → `ExportService.generate`.\n\n- Mutation — `src/exports/export.resolver.ts`: `ExportResolver.requestExport` accepts positional `accountId`, `format`, and `requestedBy` GraphQL arguments, constructs the request object, enqueues it, and returns the job ID.\n- Queue producer — `src/exports/export.producer.ts`: `ExportProducer.enqueue` accepts `ExportJob` and adds it unchanged to queue `exports` under job name `generate-export`.\n- Job contract — `src/exports/jobs/export.job.ts`: `ExportJob` defines the shared payload: `{ accountId: string; format: \"csv\" | \"json\"; requestedBy: string }`.\n- Consumer — `src/exports/export.processor.ts`: `ExportProcessor.process` consumes `Job<ExportJob>` from queue `exports` and forwards `job.data` unchanged.\n- Terminal field consumer — `src/exports/export.service.ts`: `ExportService.generate` reads `accountId` and `format` to build `/exports/{accountId}.{format}`. It is affected if fields move/rename or format semantics change.\n- Tests — `test/exports/export-flow.test.ts`: the sole export-flow test directly calls the mutation with the old positional format and constructs the old BullMQ `data` payload. Its invocation, fixture, and expected output path must track the new format. It does not currently assert the payload passed to `producer.enqueue`.\n\nThus, a request-shape change directly requires updating the resolver, `ExportJob`, service field access where applicable, and the flow test. The producer and processor are behaviorally opaque pass-through layers, but their `ExportJob`-typed signatures make them part of the affected compile-time contract.",
    "reportedFiles": [
